From 66166dffd07475f68357da28f0de68dc374e304d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:09:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ThaiWordBreak: faster dictionary lookups

Finding the words starting at each position of a Thai run was done
with two binary searches per char over the sorted word list: a third
of the instructions spent opening a big Thai book went there.

Use a trie in flat arrays instead (children of a node are consecutive,
with a direct table for the first two chars), and keep all per-node
data of a run in a single array.

Same results (checked on a 8.7M chars Thai novel, with and without
user words, and on random text): Thai word breaking uses 47% fewer
instructions, rendering of that book 21% fewer. The main word list
takes about 0.8 MB more memory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WnQiwJWG9cTSRdhDEdqpmR
